31. What is Delta Lake and why is it important?
Delta Lake is a storage layer built on top of Parquet that adds ACID transactions, schema enforcement, and time travel. It solves problems like data corruption, duplicate writes, and inconsistent reads — making your pipelines reliable and production-ready.
32. What are the key features of Delta Lake?
	• ACID transactions
	• Schema enforcement
	• Time travel (versioned data)
	• MERGE/UPSERT support
	• Scalable metadata handling
33. How does Delta Lake support ACID transactions?
Delta Lake uses a transaction log (_delta_log) to track changes. Every write is atomic, consistent, isolated, and durable — just like a database. This prevents partial writes or corrupted data.
34. What is time travel in Delta Lake?
Time travel lets you query older versions of a Delta table using a timestamp or version number:
sql
SELECT * FROM my_table VERSION AS OF 5
This helps with debugging, audits, and rollback.
35. How do you implement upserts using Delta Lake?
Use the MERGE INTO command:
sql
MERGE INTO target_table USING source_table
ON target_table.id = source_table.id
WHEN MATCHED THEN UPDATE ...
WHEN NOT MATCHED THEN INSERT ...
This updates existing rows and inserts new ones — perfect for incremental loads.
